Sorry for late response. There is not only piggybacked (ACK and, for robustness, CON and NON_CON) and separate responses (CON and NON_CON), but also empty ACK and RESET which do not carry tokens even though the request did.

Here is the test and the fix I prepared. I tried to tackle also:
- MID = 0 and no token
- Token-len is different, but content is equal, i.e. if comparing the shorter len, the compare results in equal despite being of different len
- MID is equal but token is not
- token is equal but MID is not

